[00:12.71] With quill and silver knife
[00:20.76] She carved a poison pen
[00:28.78] Wrote to her lover's wife
[00:36.26] "Your husband's seed has fed my flesh"
[00:45.05] As if a leper's face
[00:52.43] That tainted letter graced
[01:00.44] The wife with choke-stone throat
[01:08.40] Ran to the day with tear-blind eyes
[01:16.42] 
[03:21.88] Impaled on nails of ice
[03:29.04] And raked with emerald fire
[03:37.19] The wife with soul of snow
[03:44.53] With steady hands, begins to write
[03:52.68] "I'm still, I need no life
[04:00.91] To serve on boys and men
[04:08.76] What's mine was yours is dead
[04:16.65] I take my leave of mortal flesh"
[04:22.76] 